[19.328, "o", "q1: Why can my friend not view my website when I send them a localhost link running on my computer?\r\n"]
[22.933, "o", "A localhost link points to your own computer, so it cannot be viewed by others because the address points to their machine, not yours [class2:localhost-is-for-testing-but-you-cant-share-it:1].\r\n"]
[22.933, "o", "q2: Each time I changed my model, I checked its score on the final test data and picked the settings with the highest score. Why can I not trust that evaluation, and which data should I use to choose settings?\r\n"]
[26.667, "o", "If you keep changing the model after seeing its test score, that score starts guiding development, so the final test set should be kept untouched until your choices are fixed [class3:keep-a-test-set-outside-development:1]. You should use validation data to choose settings [class3:keep-a-test-set-outside-development:1].\r\n"]
[26.667, "o", "q3: What is an embedding, and how does vector-search-based RAG use embeddings to find documents relevant to a question? Does this process retrain the answering model?\r\n"]
[32.647, "o", "An embedding represents a word as a vector, where nearby vectors capture related meanings; for example, the vectors for \"dog\" and \"puppy\" are close because they have related meanings [class4:distance-becomes-a-retrieval-primitive:1]. Vector-search-based RAG uses embeddings stored in a vector database to find document chunks that are near the question's meaning [class5:vector-databases-search-by-meaning:1]. This process adds context to the question and does not retrain the answering model [class5:building-a-tiny-rag-demo:1].\r\n"]
[32.648, "o", "q4: What is the actual measured average response time, in seconds, of local Gemma searching these five lectures on my laptop?\r\n"]
[34.662, "o", "The provided source passages do not contain information about the actual measured average response time of local Gemma searching lectures on a laptop.\r\n"]
